---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../styles/global.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<Layout title="Glorious Chariot" active="Hangar">
  <section class="detail-hero"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div class="detail-copy"><p class="kicker">Hangar file 01 // ownership disputed</p><h1>Glorious<br />Chariot</h1><p class="lede">A luxury 3000-class space yacht built by SoroSuub, customised for Darga the Hutt, and acquired by us after his death. The handover was not peaceful.</p><div class="stamp">GLORIOUS CHARIOT<br />STATUS: OPERATIONAL / PRIVATEER<br />CREW: 1 + PASSENGERS: 10<br />CURRENT OWNER: THE CREW, APPARENTLY</div></div><img class="detail-image" src={`${base}images/glorious-chariot.png`} alt="The Glorious Chariot on its reinforced landing bay" /></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="page-wrap detail-grid"><div><p class="kicker">Manifest</p><h2>Built for decadence.<br />Refitted for survival.</h2><p class="lede" style="margin-top:24px">Darga’s original interior was once very nice. Then it became a den of iniquity, a maintenance problem, and finally our responsibility. We kept the useful parts, removed the rest, and added armour where the hull looked too optimistic.</p><div class="spec-table"><div class="spec-row"><span>Class</span><strong>Luxury 3000 space yacht</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Capacity</span><strong>1 crew / 10 passengers</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Cargo</span><strong>100 tons, plus whatever Maurice refuses to leave behind</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Hyperdrive</span><strong>Class 2 / backup class 14</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Defence</span><strong>Shields, armour, flush hardpoints, plausible deniability</strong></div><div class="spec-row"><span>Acquisition</span><strong>Darga died. We took the keys.</strong></div></div></div><div class="plate about-card"><p class="kicker">Crew assessment</p><h3>“It has a cargo hatch now.”</h3><p style="margin-top:20px">The Chariot is our showpiece, our refuge, and the clearest sign that subtlety did not survive the handover. It carries ten passengers, a serious amount of kit, and the confidence of a ship that now has a properly sized landing pad.</p><p>Do not ask what happened to the previous owner. The answer is in the travelogue.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
